require vs. import: The Two Module Systems
You are right to be suspicious. This is an issue of mismatched code from different eras of Node.js.

require() belongs to the older CommonJS (CJS) module system. It was the original way Node.js handled modules.

import belongs to the modern ECMAScript Modules (ESM) system. This is the official standard for JavaScript now, and it's what the rest of your Swerver.js file is using.

The line require('dotenv').config() is a very common one-liner from the CJS era. For consistency and to avoid potential issues in your ESM-based project, you should change it.

The modern import way to do this is:

JavaScript

// At the very top of Swerver.js
import dotenv from 'dotenv';
dotenv.config();
