Your placement of the code is logical, but it has one important side effect. The way it's written now, const directoryIndex = fs.readdirSync(swerverRootPath); runs only once when the server starts. This means your index will be a static snapshot and will never update if you add or remove files while the server is running.

To make it a truly live index that gets fresh data on every request, we just need to move that one line inside the API route handler.

